\end{aligned}
$$

This gradient is nonzero. Divide it by its magnitude; the common exponential factor is positive and cancels:

$$
\begin{aligned}\mathbf n&=\frac{\nabla f(\frac{\pi}{2},\frac{\pi}{6})}{\|\nabla f(\frac{\pi}{2},\frac{\pi}{6})\|} \\ &=\frac{\left(-1 + \sqrt{3}\right)\,i+\left(- \sqrt{3} - 1\right)\,j}{2 \sqrt{2}} \\ &=\left(- \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} + \frac{\sqrt{6}}{4}\right)\,i+\left(- \frac{\sqrt{6}}{4} - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4}\right)\,j
\end{aligned}
